[{"code":"list_still_used","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":12,"col":12},"end":{"line":12,"col":28}},"title":"LIST CHANGED WHILE STILL IN USE","message":"`List.push` changes `rows` in place, but `count`, a function that holds the\nlist, is used afterwards.\n\n11|    count = λ⊤ → List.length rows\n       ^^^^^ `count` holds the list here\n12|    more = List.push rows r\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n13|    count ⊤ + List.length more\n       ^^^^^ and `count` is used here, after the change\n\nIf the list were changed in place, `count` would see the change when it is used\non line 13.\n\nTo change a copy and leave `rows` as it was, copy it there:\n\n12|    more = List.push (List.copy rows) r\n\nThis is sharing the checker can see: `count` is used on line 13, after the\nchange."}]
